.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH GENETREE 1 2000-1月 "make_profile" "make_profile"
.SH NAME
make_profile \- Create the training/solving configuration profile of the GeneTree model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fImake_profile(\fBprofile\fR as <integer> GeneTreeProfile = [Fast], 
\fBpopulation\fR as integer = 100, 
\fBiterations\fR as integer = 60, 
\fBcells\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmax_genes\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmax_regulators\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBinclude_undirected\fR as boolean = TRUE);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create the training/solving configuration profile of the GeneTree model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBprofile\fB \fR\- 
 the performance profile: \fBfast\fR (at most 1000 cells per model, top 10
 regulators, 40 boosting rounds), \fBbalanced\fR (3000 cells, top 20 regulators,
 100 rounds) or \fBfull\fR (all of the cells and all of the regulators).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpopulation\fB \fR\- 
 the number of cells that are used as the independent initial states of the
 damped fixed point iteration, more cells give a more reliable population
 level statistic but cost more time.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBiterations\fB \fR\- the maximum iteration rounds of the fixed point solving.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcells\fB \fR\- 
 the maximum number of cells that is used by each gene model, \fB0\fR keeps the
 value of the selected profile.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_genes\fB \fR\- 
 only the first n target genes(ordered by the regulator count in descending
 order) are trained, \fB0\fR means all of the target genes.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_regulators\fB \fR\- 
 the number of the regulators that is kept for each target gene(the top n
 regulator ordered by the mutual information in descending order), a negative
 value keeps the value of the selected profile, \fB0\fR keeps all of them.
. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the [GeneTreeConfig](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.GeneTree.GeneTreeConfig) configuration object.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneTree
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
